A||N||17||Ozzy||Code 32 Blues!||||5||
Z||000000||Ozzy||04-13-2000||10:43 AM||||Well, here come the little signals from the V-6 saying "Give me attention!!! Spend lottsa money on meeeeeeeee!!"<P>Driving around yesterday and SES light comes on. Checked the code last night. Code 32 EGR yada, yada, yada! It had a new EGR tube installed at the dealer ship I bought it from. I had all that stuff off doing the exhaust manafolds and noticed the tube is kinda tuff to get in place at the EGR end for a tight seal but I cleaned it up and I'm pretty sure I have it sealed. Could this be related??<P>This morning driving to work I pushed it pretty good going up a hill to pass and then it started running like crap at the lower end. It will rev but needs more throttle than usual. SES came on again but am at work right now (7:35am) and have not had a chance to check. It did not run crappy after the code 32 set yesterday.<P>Gimme some places to look guys. This V-6 if such a different beast compared to my Iron Puke...<P>Thanx in adv...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tom88gt||04-13-2000||12:19 PM||||Its your EGR solenoid.  Very pricey, almost $100.  It appears several of us are having code 32 problems.  I havn't replaced mine yet.  I just can't believe it costs so much.  Its just a typical 2.8 GM engine.  Millions of them on the road.  Why does the Fiero's cost so much more?  Does it have a special valve?  I'm holding out.  Hopefully I'll find one in a junkyard for $5.  Most auto parts stores don't even have it.<P>Has anyone found a reasonable price for this item?||||reg||9
Z||000002||mshill||04-13-2000||12:20 PM||||I also have the code 32 blues, but it only comes on at speeds higher than 75 mph and even that varies.  I have checked all my vacuum lines, done the EGR test using a vacuum pump.  The only thing I have not done is clean the filter out on the EGR solenoid.  That's next.  Then if it happens again, I don't know what I will do.  When mine triggers the code 32 it does not run any different.  I do get pretty poor gas mileage<BR>(16 city) but I also have a +1 cam in it.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000003||Ozzy||04-13-2000||12:36 PM||||Hey guys...Dunno what is going on right now.<P>Just went and checked the code I got this morning and now it is showing a 33! MAP sensor. I could have sworn I had a 32 last night and I have NOT cleared the codes! I have never heard of a code dissapearing. They usually remain in memory right? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Guess I need to check out the map sensor. I have a connector that is supect on the MAP so I will investigate further.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||04-13-2000||02:58 PM||||I think the MAP sensor is a more likely suspect here.  I get a code 32 after a few minutes of freeway driving, but it doesn't affect performance in any way.  I just don't feel like putting out the money for a new solenoid...||||reg||1
