Z||000008||fieroshop||04-14-2000||12:47 AM||||It has been my experience that if you replace a sensor with a used sensor more then likely you have a fifty fifty chance of getting a good sensor. Unfortunatly everytime I bought a replaced a sensor wit a used sensor I have had to replace it with a new one because the used were all bad. Ozzy if you can't find a sensor I have them in stock.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ozzy||04-14-2000||01:05 AM||||Hey there George!  No I don't want to buy 2nd hand sensors. I was just curious what AL meant. BTW, I fixed up that exhaust and emergency brake lever. Starting to get my 'Blue beast' together! Thnx for the deal. ;D<P>Guys, I checked the MAP sensor connector and pushed it back in. It has a broken clip. It was not out really but may have been the problem. It's running fine at the moment so I guess I'll see.<P>Sure is sweet when its running good. Man, I can't imagine what these cars are like with 200 hp! <P>Ozzy||||reg||1
