Z||000011||Gokart||04-14-2000||08:37 PM||||Just fixed my code 32 woes...no hoax this time, it was the solenoid! The coolant smell I had was also related. The cap wasn't on tight enough and coolant was dripping on the solenoid probably frying it! So instead of taking it out and cleaning it or finding a used replacement I broked down and paid $84.95 to the Fiero Store's. WHAT A DIFFERENCE! Runs like a top again! I'm thinking a making some kind of shroud made of metal flashing to attach to the thermostat housing that will be over the solenoid protecting it from rain/moisture.||||reg||14
Z||000012||Fiasco||04-14-2000||08:52 PM||||Get it fixed, Ozzy?<BR>One thing I do know is that if you're not sure the EGR tube is sealing properly, I would check again. When I got my 85, the tube was badly cracked and just moving it by hand back and forth would change the idle dramatically.<BR>Also, I cleaned out the solenoid's filter on mine and the code 32 went away... but only for about a week...<P>FIEROSHOP- What do you get for a vac. reg. solenoid???? ($$$)||||reg||1
Z||000013||AL||04-14-2000||10:13 PM||||well for 5 bucks i rather take that 50/ 50 chance plus you can always clean and change the filter on the 5 buck solenoid, now if your rich and single and don't have a wife and kids then go ahead and spend that extra 100 dollars.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ozzy||04-15-2000||12:47 AM||||So AL...Do you have a solenoid your selling for $5.00 or do you have a supply of cheaper solenoids?<P>I'll bite. For $5.00 I can have a spare...<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000015||AL||04-15-2000||01:45 AM||||hey ozz five bucks is what i spent on buying it at the junkyard,it doesn't include the labor i spent on finding and taking them off plus the gas i spend on the junkyard trips,now if you think any body will sell you one for the exact price he paid for it you are mistaken, now if you want to make a junkyard trip and pay 5 bucks for it be my guest, but you won't get it at that price when all you have to do is sit in your chair and say i'll bite.you guys have a good weekend,   and go out and find your parts, it'sfun to find those special items,AL.||||reg||10
Z||000016||Gokart||04-15-2000||06:01 AM||||Oz, I always try the parts from my parts car first to save $. Tried the solenoid from it and it ran worse than before! I got a wife and kids, and I'm learning you can actually WASTE more money fooling with "cheap" fixes before finally breaking down and doing the Fiero justice! Wish everyone could hear and feel the difference the new solenoid makes. <p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 04-15-2000).]||||reg||2
